---
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ProductHero from "@/components/products/ProductHero.astro";
import ProductCTA from "@/components/products/ProductCTA.astro";
import FAQList from "@/components/ui/FAQList.astro";
import { resolveProductCommerce } from "@/lib/lemon-squeezy";

const products = await getCollection("products");
const product = products.find((item) => item.data.slug === "developer-marketing-quickstart");
if (!product) throw new Error("Developer Marketing Quickstart product entry was not found.");
const commerce = resolveProductCommerce(product.data);

const steps = [
  {
    title: "Pick one kind of business you can reach.",
    body: 'Not "small businesses" in general. A specific type you can find, contact, and understand.',
  },
  {
    title: "Find a problem that costs them money.",
    body: "Something they'd pay to fix, so the conversation starts with their business instead of your tech stack.",
  },
  {
    title: "Turn it into a simple offer.",
    body: "A first version of what you'd sell. Clear enough to test; it doesn't need to be final.",
  },
  {
    title: "Build your First 25.",
    body: "A short list of businesses that actually fit, so you're not messaging strangers at random.",
  },
  {
    title: "Reach out and record what happens.",
    body: "Send messages built around the problem you've investigated, then log every reply, question, and no.",
  },
  {
    title: "Decide what to change.",
    body: "Adjust the buyer, the problem, or the offer based on what happened, not on guesses.",
  },
];

const faqs = [
  {
    data: {
      order: 1,
      question: "Do I need a niche or a portfolio first?",
      answer: "No. Choosing who to reach is step one, and the process works with the useful work you've already done.",
    },
  },
  {
    data: {
      order: 2,
      question: "I hate cold outreach. Is this for me?",
      answer: "Probably more than most. Cold outreach feels bad when it's generic. Here, every message starts with a specific business and a problem you've actually investigated, so you're not sending the same pitch to strangers.",
    },
  },
  {
    data: {
      order: 3,
      question: "How long does it take?",
      answer: "The Quickstart uses a seven-day activation plan to get your first client-acquisition cycle into motion. Seven days is not a promise that a client will appear within a week; it's a structure for choosing the buyer, building the offer and First 25, making real market contact, and knowing what to do next.",
    },
  },
  {
    data: {
      order: 4,
      question: "Why is it free?",
      answer: "It's the first step in the Developer Business Lab system. It lets you use the approach before deciding whether you need the deeper paid systems for pricing, sales, delivery, and growth.",
    },
  },
  {
    data: {
      order: 5,
      question: "Why does it go through a checkout page?",
      answer: "Lemon Squeezy handles delivery and emails you the download link after checkout. The product price is $0.",
    },
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Developer Marketing Quickstart | Free Guide + Workbook"
  description="Build your First 25, put a clear offer in front of real buyers, and get your first deliberate client-acquisition cycle moving with this free guide and workbook."
  enableCheckoutOverlay={commerce.purchasable}
>
  <ProductHero
    product={product}
    breadcrumbs={[]}
    eyebrow="Free guide and workbook for freelance developers"
    title="Your next client probably isn't hiding in your portfolio."
    description="You already know how to do the work. The Developer Marketing Quickstart shows you how to create opportunities to get paid for it: choose one buyer, find a problem worth solving, shape an offer, build your First 25, and put it in front of real businesses. In seven days, you'll have your first client-acquisition cycle in motion and real market feedback instead of guesses."
    ctaLabel="Get the Free Quickstart"
    supportingText="Free. Enter your email on the next screen and it's yours."
    location="free-hero"
  />

  <section class="border-y border-border bg-card/35 px-6 py-18 sm:px-6 sm:py-24 lg:px-8">
    <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-7xl gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[.72fr_1.28fr] lg:gap-20">
      <div><h2 class="text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">You're good at the work. Getting the work is the part nobody taught you.</h2></div>
      <div class="space-y-5 text-lg leading-8 text-muted-foreground">
        <p>Your clients come from referrals, a platform, or an agency. When they send work, you're busy. When they don't, you wait.</p>
        <p>You've told yourself you'll start finding clients once the portfolio is done. It's been almost done for a while.</p>
        <p>You've written cold emails in your head. Every one sounded like spam, so none of them got sent.</p>
        <p>A project starts winding down and the math starts running in your head. <em>What's coming in next month? Who replaces this client? How long can I afford an empty calendar?</em></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="px-6 py-18 sm:px-6 sm:py-24 lg:px-8">
    <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-7xl gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[.72fr_1.28fr] lg:gap-20">
      <div><h2 class="text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Treat it like a first build, not a launch.</h2></div>
      <div class="space-y-5 text-lg leading-8 text-muted-foreground">
        <p>You'd never spend three months on a feature without shipping a test version. Finding clients works the same way.</p>
        <p>You don't need the perfect niche, website, or pitch before you start. You need a small version you can put in front of people, and their response tells you what to change.</p>
        <p class="font-semibold text-foreground">You don't need to become a salesperson. You need to know who you're contacting, why they might care, and what you're asking them to do next.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="border-y border-border bg-card/35 px-6 py-18 sm:px-6 sm:py-24 lg:px-8">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl">
      <p class="editorial-kicker">What you'll do</p>
      <h2 class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">One round of finding clients, start to finish</h2>
      <div class="mt-10 grid gap-px overflow-hidden border border-border bg-border md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
        {steps.map((step) => (
          <article class="bg-background p-7">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold">{step.title}</h3>
            <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-muted-foreground">{step.body}</p>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="px-6 py-18 sm:px-6 sm:py-24 lg:px-8">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl">
      <div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[.72fr_1.28fr] lg:gap-20">
        <div><h2 class="text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">What you get</h2></div>
        <div class="space-y-6 text-lg leading-8 text-muted-foreground">
          <p><strong class="text-foreground">The 64-page guide</strong> walks you through each step, from choosing a buyer to reading the results of your first outreach cycle.</p>
          <p><strong class="text-foreground">The 45-page workbook</strong> is where you make every decision as you go: your buyer, their problem, your offer, your First 25 prospects, what happened when you reached out, and what you'll change next. When you finish, it becomes the working record for round two.</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-foreground">By the end, you'll have chosen a market, built an offer, identified 25 real prospects, contacted them, and collected actual market feedback instead of guessing what might work.</p>
          <p><strong class="text-foreground">This is the client-acquisition starting point.</strong> It doesn't try to teach the entire freelance business. The goal is simpler: help you stop waiting for work and run your first deliberate attempt to find it.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="border-y border-border bg-card/35 px-6 py-18 sm:px-6 sm:py-24 lg:px-8">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl">
      <h2 class="text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-8"><FAQList faqs={faqs} /></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="px-6 py-18 sm:px-6 sm:py-24 lg:px-8">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl text-center">
      <h2 class="text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">Your next client won't come from another portfolio redesign.</h2>
      <p class="mx-auto mt-6 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-8 text-muted-foreground">Build your First 25. Put your offer in front of real buyers. Give yourself a way to create opportunities instead of waiting for them.</p>
      <div class="mt-8 flex justify-center"><ProductCTA product={product} location="free-final" label="Get the Free Quickstart" /></div>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-muted-foreground">Free. Enter your email on the next screen and it's yours.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
